  "language": "english",
  "text": "They analyze on the slow queries, and the problem is a missing composite index on the orders table, on customer ID, and created that. Someone dropped it during the schema migration with Alembic. Ouch! Is there a fix ready? Yes. I wrote a new migration that recreates the index concurrently, so it will not lock the  SQL. I also added a check in our CI pipeline, using pgstat statements, so we get an alert in Datadog if any query goes above 200 milliseconds. That's really helpful. From the product side, customers definitely noticed. We had 11 support tickets about slow checkout in the last week, and our NPS score dropped by 3 points. Thanks, Aisha. Okay, item 3, the Q3OKRs. Aisha, can you give us the summary?",
